  "relationship": "Independent native interception and host callback ownership follow the pinned precedence, registration, continuation, removal and header contracts. No upstream browser driver is used for candidate routing.",
  "changes": [
    "Immutable occurrence joins and bounded shared native pause/body ownership replace upstream channel objects.",
    "Only typed Fetch body fields use the bounded binary-input writer; generic control limits remain unchanged.",
    "Host history evicts whole redirect chains and accounts for lazy body/header growth. External user references remain valid.",
    "Callback scopes prevent a removed handler from claiming a later handling stage. User registration async context and original error stacks are preserved.",
    "Route.fetch and APIResponse-backed fulfillment remain unsupported. Original request observation has independent event limits; 32 MiB output bodies do not establish 32 MiB original-request or redirect observation."
